./.lattice/story/actives/B-bf52/review-runs.json:15:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"c916bc0a53f4c1465a605def7d6cde3601c5843e8b61475d73fa1a9b0a4d8742\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review verification intent and evidence coverage.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"9845080b4d332e675cced9230749066c0a72bab5e830d54417c7f6206a5e7dc7\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/convergence-breaker.ts:479 truncates the normalized reason to 200 characters before hashing. ProofStory gap lists share a preamble longer than that, so two different gaps hash identically. Hash the full normalized reason, retaining only a large sanity bound to cap CPU on pathological input.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/convergence-breaker.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/convergence-breaker-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Remove the fixed-length truncation so late-diverging rejection reasons keep distinct digests\",\"userSees\":\"node packages/main/dist/tasks/convergence-breaker-smoke.js prints a passing check stating that two real DEV-gate rejection renders differing only past the former 200-character cut produce different digest keys.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Restoring only the fixed-length truncation makes the new smoke assertions fail, proving the check is bound to this change and not to some unrelated property.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"A rejection reason far longer than any realistic gate message still produces a digest, and the retained sanity bound is exercised rather than silently absent.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Two reasons that are identical up to the sanity bound and differ only beyond it are documented as collapsing, so the bound's residual behavior is stated rather than assumed away.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:1\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"gateFailureDigest applied to two reconstructions of the real DEV-gate rejection render (machine.ts:179 preamble plus renderProofStoryDiagnosticReport), identical for their first 244 normalized characters and differing only in the outstanding gap codes, returns two different keys.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"The same two rejections routed through bumpGateFailureCount leave maxGateFailureCount at 1, so assessBreaker does not trip, which is the actual operator-visible consequence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:1\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/convergence-breaker.ts:475 rewrites any slash-bearing token, collapsing DEV/REVIEW with DEV/TEST and src/core/alpha.ts with src/core/beta.ts. Restrict it to absolute paths anchored at machine-specific roots so relative repo paths and slash-bearing identifiers stay distinct while host-varying paths still collapse.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/convergence-breaker.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/convergence-breaker-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Narrow the path normalizer to machine-specific absolute roots only\",\"userSees\":\"The convergence-breaker smoke prints passing checks stating that DEV/REVIEW and DEV/TEST digest differently, that two files under a shared first path segment digest differently, and that the same lock path under /Users and under /private/var still digests identically.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Restoring the greedy slash-anchored regex makes the new distinctness checks fail while the machine-path collapse check keeps passing, proving both directions are independently bound to this change.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"The same logical lock path rendered under a machine-specific root (/Users/... versus /private/var/...) still produces one digest key, so host-varying paths keep collapsing.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"A path that begins at a machine-specific root but continues into repo-relative segments is normalized once, without leaving a partially-rewritten remainder that could differ per host.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:1\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Two rejection reasons differing only in a slash-bearing identifier (the phase pair DEV/REVIEW versus DEV/TEST) produce different digest keys.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Two rejection reasons naming different repo-relative files under a shared first segment (src/core/alpha.ts versus src/core/beta.ts) produce different digest keys.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:1\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/convergence-breaker.ts:476 rewrites digit runs inside identifier tokens, collapsing CHK-001 with CHK-002. Restrict it so digits attached to an identifier survive while free-standing counters such as attempt numbers still collapse.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":